-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       Ghosts 'n Goblins
  Publisher   Elite, 1986
  Version     1.6

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch:

  File        Ghosts 'n Goblins (1986)(Elite Systems)[aka Ghost 'n
              Goblins].z80
  MD5         23d69f517506104c36ba429cb2148fa5

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  Moving figures become Next hardware sprites, so they keep their own colours
  and no longer take on the scenery's (colour clash). Game logic is unchanged.

  Colours     Default (the game's own) plus: Enhanced, chosen on the menu, off
              by default.
  Enhanced    Owner-painted flat colours on the original Spectrum drawings,
              chosen from an arcade reference; armour, faces, zombies and
              graves painted, climbing poses included. Excess black padding
              trimmed from unarmoured Arthur. White HUD text and cyan weapon
              on black. Source: Enhanced colours: Jon Attree.

  Pace        original

  Changes     1.6: the moving platform over the water no longer glitches with
              Always the dagger on (the cheat corrupted one of its four
              drawings)
              1.5: real cheats (invincibility; start at level 2 or 3; always
              the dagger); infinite time no longer stops the game from
              starting
              1.4: figures move through intermediate positions between the
              game's two-frame steps; a zombie's pot no longer shows below
              ground as it emerges; latest owner sprite painting in Enhanced.
              Game logic, sound and delays unchanged.

  Note        0 starts/fires; 5 left, 8 right, 7 up, 6 down, SPACE jump. J
              joystick, R redefine. Enhanced off by default. Original pace and
              loading screen. Known issues: in one spot on level 3 a ladder
              can blink for a frame as the scenery scrolls (the sprite engine
              delays the game's redraw of it until after the screen has been
              drawn there); the original does not do this; a fix is planned.
              The mean pace is within 0.3% of the original's, but short
              stretches with sound measured up to 7.5% slower. Missing:
              Enhanced colours for the scenery (planned); not yet checked: the
              ending, the late bosses, joystick and redefine; hardware
              untested.

-- MENU ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   1  Infinite lives
   2  Infinite time
   3  Invincibility
   4  Start at level 2
   5  Start at level 3
   6  Always the dagger

  Infinite lives is the archive's POKE for this release; the other cheats were
  found in the game's code for this patch, and Infinite time replaces the
  archive's, which stopped the game from starting.

