-- TESTING -------------------------------------------------------------------
  Tested      Played by the owner in JNext 2026-11-06 (1.4 colours and engine,
              1.5 cheats): approved; the 1.6 platform fix checked in the
              simulator and headless JNext

  Replay      Both sets: 11 recordings, 53063 frames each, identical game
              state, registers, positions and 331570 exact painted patterns;
              every hook ran (125170 plots, 139028 object hooks, 24223 draw
              passes, 24209 Copper commits). Carried-pot oracle: 567 hidden,
              960 partial, 1517 full. Per set 648 clipping cases and 3120
              clock/R/IFF cases (incl. 2048 object hook). 34 replay, 5
              clipping/atlas and 1 stale-history negative controls caught.

  Emulator    JNext headless: per set a 5000-frame death/reset run (8 reset
              hooks, no Copper update during sprite drawing) and native pot-
              emergence captures; actual loader rebuilt both sets byte for
              byte from private card-image copies. Hardware untested.

  Coverage    152 complete painted images, 315 recorded/audited variants. Six
              injected section-start fixtures (c0-c10; c6 is not a valid
              start); natural death, game over and menus; both climbing forms;
              a natural zombie pot emergence. Ending, late bosses, joystick
              and redefine paths remain uncovered. v1.5 cheats: 9 cheat
              recordings (43,030 frames) replay identical in both sets; level
              2 and 3 starts played through their first scroll; JNext runs of
              each cheat; 15-minute all-cheats soak. v1.6: the dagger cheat
              fixed; 4 more recordings (19,174 frames, incl. a ride on the
              water platform) replay identical in both sets; the platform
              drawings stay intact.

  Hardware    none

  Nothing here claims a result on real hardware unless the line above says so.

-- HOW TO USE ----------------------------------------------------------------
  Put this .nxc and the game file in the same folder on the Next's card and
  choose the .nxc in the Browser. See README.txt.
